    "caption": "For those days when you’re craving an indulgent, garlicky beef bowl, head over to #TheMarketplace, grab some Margaret River Wagyu Beef Cubes, and prepare this Garlic Butter Wagyu Steak Rice!\n\nThe irresistible combination of fatty wagyu, punchy garlic, and earthy mushrooms drenched with a rich, golden egg yolk makes this dish both comforting and filling. Why not give it a shot this weekend? Enjoy!\n\nServing Time: 30 minutes\nYield: 2 servings\n\nIngredients\n\n1 tbsp. olive oil\n250g Margaret River Wagyu Beef Cubes, pat-dried\n1/2 tsp. salt\n1/4 tsp. black pepper\n2 tbsps. butter\n6 cloves garlic, thinly sliced\n1 cup cooked Japanese rice\n1/4 cup chopped shiitake mushrooms\n1/4 cup frozen green peas\n1 egg yolk, for garnish\n¼ cup leeks, thinly sliced, for garnish\n\nProcedure\n\n1. Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.\n2. Season the Wagyu steak with salt and pepper.\n3. Add the Wagyu steak to the skillet and cook for 2-3 minutes per side, or until cooked to desired doneness. Remove the Wagyu steak from the skillet and set aside.\n4. Reduce the heat to medium. Add the butter and garlic to the skillet. Cook the garlic for 1 minute, or until fragrant.Add the rice, shiitake mushrooms, and green peas to the skillet.\n5. Cook the rice for 2-3 minutes, or until heated through.\n6. Serve the rice topped with the Wagyu steak, egg yolk, and leeks.\n\nOrder your groceries online at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceGoCart. Join our Viber community as well at https://bit.ly/TheMarketplaceViber!",
